To apply the change, use `fix_at_line`:
- Call `file_editor view` first with a `view_range` around the problem lines listed below — you need the current content.
- Then call `fix_at_line` with `start_line` / `end_line` set to the inclusive range you are replacing (equal values for a single-line fix), `old_block` set to the current content of that range (exactly as `view` showed it), and `new_block` set to the replacement (with correct indentation).
- `fix_at_line` anchors by line number, so duplicated lines elsewhere in the file will not cause failures.
- Do NOT use `file_editor str_replace` — it is unsafe when the file has duplicated lines.

